# Code Organization

## File Structure Standards

- Separate into: **components**, **utils**, **hooks**, **types** per `@prd.txt`
- **Maximum 240 lines per file** — break into smaller files if exceeded
- Use TypeScript for all code files
- **Avoid `any`** — use proper TypeScript typing

## Package Management

- **Use `yarn`** for all dependency management and commands
- Do not use `npm` or `pnpm`

## Backend, Validation & Data Fetching

- Backend source of truth is the **project API** (see `src/lib/api/` and `src/services/`)
- Use the project's migration tooling for all schema changes
- Any DB schema change MUST include a migration and rollback note
- Use **zod** for request/response/form validation
- Use **`@src/lib/apiHandler`** for all HTTP/API calls — only inside `services/*.service.ts`, not in hooks or components
- Every API call path MUST handle loading, error, and empty states
- Use **React Query** for server state
- Define query keys in **`@/constants/queryKeys.ts`** — import `QUERY_KEYS` in every API hook/mutation

## Mandatory DO

- Break EVERY prompt into tasks; update `todo.md` before starting
- Mark progress immediately; work sequentially; clear `todo.md` when done
- Check `/components/ui` before creating UI
- Use `ConfirmDeleteDialog` for delete confirmations
- Ask before creating new shared components
- Keep files under 240 lines; use proper TypeScript typing
- Use `yarn`, `zod`, `@src/lib/apiHandler`, React Query, query key factory
- Place all tests under `tests/` mirroring `src/` — never add `*.test.ts(x)` inside `src/`

## Mandatory DON'T

- Skip task breakdown or work without updating `todo.md`
- Work on multiple tasks simultaneously
- Create components outside `/components/ui` without asking
- Use `any`, `npm`, `pnpm`, or files exceeding 240 lines
- Add `*.test.ts` or `*.test.tsx` files inside `src/` — use `tests/` instead
- Call APIs directly from components without `apiHandler`
- Put `fetch*` / `get*` API logic inside hook files — use `services/<action>.service.ts`
- Add response `*Mapper.ts` in module `utils/` when `@/shared/types/dtos/` already matches the API — use DTO fields in UI
- Merge DB changes without migration + rollback notes
- Leave API paths without loading/error/empty-state handling
- Define ad-hoc React Query keys outside `@/constants/queryKeys.ts`
- Use inline string literals in `queryKey` / `invalidateQueries` — use `QUERY_KEYS` from `@/constants/queryKeys`
- Use `window.confirm` for destructive actions
